; NextDAAD sprite animation fixture. STIMULUS fixture: tests\build-tests.ps1
; asserts the compiled bytes; tests\sprites_dump.py drives it over ZRCP and
; reads the DEBUG snapshot after every ANYKEY. Sets: 002 torch 8-bit,
; 003 32x32 one-shot, 006 4-bit two blocks, 015 8-bit in block 2, 020-028
; copies of 002 for the record ceiling.
;
; MOUSE 0 1 shows the pointer so the pointer mask and the pointer-over-4-bit
; check are live. PICTURE 1 needs a picture file: the -Sprites leg stages the
; palette card as 001.NX2. S11's behaviour arrives in Task 9.
;
; ANYKEY, not PAUSE 0: it is the V2 wait-for-key condact and behaves the same
; whether or not -v3 is given, so the fixture does not depend on the header
; version. SYSMESS 16 carries a trailing #n so the next MESSAGE starts on its
; own line.

/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
SOUTH  3  noun
LOOK   4  verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key.#n"
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "S1 GFX 2 19#n"
/1 "S2 GFX 6 19#n"
/2 "S3 GFX 15 19 refused: block 2 claimed#n"
/3 "S4 GFX 6 21#n"
/4 "S5 GFX 15 19 cache hit#n"
/5 "S6 GFX 255 21#n"
/6 "S7 GFX 100 20 set 3 at 40,100#n"
/7 "S8 GFX 253 20 refused#n"
/8 "S9 eight starts then a ninth#n"
/9 "S10 restart of a live set#n"
/10 "S11 PICTURE stops all#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The sprite lab."
/CON
/0
NORTH 1
/1
SOUTH 0
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   MOUSE 0 1
        GFX 2 19
        MESSAGE 0
        ANYKEY
        GFX 6 19
        MESSAGE 1
        ANYKEY
        GFX 15 19
        MESSAGE 2
        ANYKEY
        GFX 6 21
        MESSAGE 3
        ANYKEY
        GFX 15 19
        MESSAGE 4
        ANYKEY
        GFX 255 21
        MESSAGE 5
        ANYKEY
        LET 100 3
        LET 101 40
        LET 102 0
        LET 103 100
        GFX 100 20
        MESSAGE 6
        ANYKEY
        GFX 253 20
        MESSAGE 7
        ANYKEY
        GFX 255 21
        GFX 20 19
        GFX 21 19
        GFX 22 19
        GFX 23 19
        GFX 24 19
        GFX 25 19
        GFX 26 19
        GFX 27 19
        GFX 28 19
        MESSAGE 8
        ANYKEY
        GFX 255 21
        GFX 2 19
        GFX 2 19
        MESSAGE 9
        ANYKEY
        PICTURE 1
        DISPLAY 0
        MESSAGE 10
        ANYKEY
        END
/END
